      "content": "Wait, you just said there's a \"consensus\" that it's a political failing rather than a viable tool. That seems like a huge stretch. A lot of economists argue that the problem isn't the tax itself, but just how we manage it. If we actually had the right enforcement and international cooperation, wouldn't it be a perfectly stable and effective way to fund social programs and fix the wealth gap? Why is the \"failure\" side presented as the consensus?",
