      "content": "The \"consensus\" is primarily among mainstream economists who warn that without coordinated global action to prevent capital flight, unilateral wealth taxes would likely provoke an \"Arms Race to the Bottom.\" Many theorists argue that the marginal tax on the ultra-wealthy rarely discourages significant investment compared to the wider societal cost of inequality. While local political consensus often fails due to entrenched lobbying and short-term political cycles, this institutional friction is distinct from the underlying economic mechanics of the tax itself.",
